## Workflow

1. Translator finds a Chinese Buddhist term in the source text
2. Clicks "+ Add Term", enters: Chinese term (required), Source, Source Content Chinese,
   Source Content English, Notes for Translator. Pinyin/Pali/Sanskrit are not entered —
   always AI-generated.
3. Claude AI generates: Pinyin, Pali, Sanskrit, and AI Translate 1/2/3. App
   auto-navigates to the Edit View for the new term.
4. All team members see the term in the table and open its Edit View
5. Members vote on any of the 6 translation options; they can also edit unlocked fields.
   If any AI Translate option is empty, the ✦ AI Translate button re-generates missing slots.
6. Leader or admin reviews vote tallies, sets Final (First) and optionally Final (Second)
7. Term is marked "finalized" and shown with a gold border in the table
8. All edits, votes, and finalizations are recorded in the Audit_Log sheet and displayed
   in the Editing History section at the bottom of every Edit View

