## Bulk CSV Import

Upload a CSV via the Add Term modal → Bulk Import tab.

**Supported columns:**

| Column         | Aliases              | Required | Behaviour                                      |
|----------------|----------------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|
| `chinese`      | `Chinese`            | Yes      | The Chinese term                               |
| `pinyin`       | `Pinyin`             | No       | If blank, AI-generated                         |
| `pali`         | `Pali`               | No       | If blank, AI-generated                         |
| `sanskrit`     | `Sanskrit`           | No       | If blank, AI-generated                         |
| `context`      | `Context`            | No       | Passed to AI as translation context hint       |
| `category`     | `Category`           | No       | Stored as-is                                   |
| `notes`        | `Notes`              | No       | Passed to AI as translator notes hint          |
| `source`       | `Source`             | No       | SourceID (e.g. `S001`); stored in Source col   |
| `trans_known`  | `TranslationKnown`, `known` | No | Known translation; stored in TranslationKnown |
| `added_by`     | `AddedBy`                   | No | Email to record as creator; defaults to the logged-in user if blank |

AI Translate 1–3 are **always** generated by Claude during import and cannot be
pre-supplied via CSV.

